#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
#, ai
msgid "Night {0} of 3"
msgstr "Usiku wa {0} kati ya 3"

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
#, ai
msgid "Follow the migration from Makkah to Madinah stage by stage, with every paragraph linked to the passage it rests on."
msgstr "Fuata hijrah kutoka Makkah hadi Madinah hatua kwa hatua, huku kila aya ikiwa imeunganishwa na kifungu inakotegemea."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "A rider on the road"
msgstr "Mpanda farasi njiani"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Quraysh had offered a reward for each of the two travellers. Suraqah ibn Malik recounts that a man came to his gathering and said he had just seen figures near the coast. Suraqah recognised who they must be, and set out after them."
msgstr "Maquraishi walikuwa wametoa zawadi kwa kila mmoja wa wasafiri hao wawili. Suraqah ibn Malik anasimulia kwamba mtu mmoja alikuja kwenye mkusanyiko wake na kusema kwamba alikuwa ametoka tu kuona watu karibu na pwani. Suraqah alitambua walikuwa nani, na akaondoka kuwafuata."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "By his own account, he came close enough to hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. Then the forelegs of his horse sank into the ground up to the knees, and he was thrown from it."
msgstr "Kwa mujibu wa simulizi yake mwenyewe, alikaribia vya kutosha kumsikia Mtume ﷺ akisoma. Kisha miguu ya mbele ya farasi wake ilizama ardhini hadi magotini, naye akaanguka kutoka kwake."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "He told them what Quraysh intended and offered them provisions. They took nothing from him and asked only that he keep their news hidden. At his request, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah wrote him a guarantee of safety on a piece of leather. Then they went on."
msgstr "Aliwaambia kile ambacho Maquraishi walikusudia na akawatolea vifaa vya safari. Hawakuchukua kitu chochote kutoka kwake na waliomba tu kwamba afiche habari zao. Kwa ombi lake, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah alimwandikia barua ya amana ya usalama kwenye kipande cha ngozi. Kisha wakaendelea na safari."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Quba: the first stop"
msgstr "Quba: kituo cha kwanza"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Then he rode on, with people walking beside him, until his camel knelt at a place in Madinah where some of the Muslims already prayed. It was a yard for drying dates."
msgstr "Kisha akapanda mnyama na kuendelea na safari, huku watu wakitembea kando yake, hadi ngamia wake alipopiga magoti mahali fulani huko Madinah ambapo baadhi ya Waislamu walikuwa tayari wakiswali. Palikuwa ni uwanja wa kukaushia tende."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Suraqah’s account records the reward offered for each of the two, and a report that figures had been seen near the coast."
msgstr "Simulizi ya Suraqah inaeleza zawadi iliyotolewa kwa kila mmoja wao, na ripoti kwamba watu walikuwa wameonekana karibu na pwani."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "It does not establish where on the route this happened, and the scene does not place it."
msgstr "Haionyeshi ni wapi hasa katika njia hii jambo hili lilitokea, na mandhari haionyeshi eneo hilo."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Suraqah describes the forelegs of his horse sinking into the ground to the knees, and being thrown."
msgstr "Suraqah anaeleza jinsi miguu ya mbele ya farasi wake ilivyozama ardhini hadi magotini, na yeye kuangushwa chini."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "This is his own first-person account. The scene shows the road, not the event or any person."
msgstr "Huu ni ushuhuda wake mwenyewe wa nafsi ya kwanza. Mandhari inaonyesha njia, si tukio lenyewe wala mtu yeyote."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "They asked only that he keep their news hidden; ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah wrote him a guarantee of safety."
msgstr "Waliomba tu kwamba afiche habari zao; ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah akamwandikia barua ya amana ya usalama."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The wording of the written guarantee is not given in this passage."
msgstr "Maneno ya barua hiyo ya amana ya usalama hayajatajwa katika kifungu hiki."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The account gives a stay of more than ten nights among Bani ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf and the founding of a mosque there."
msgstr "Simulizi inataja kukaa kwa zaidi ya usiku kumi miongoni mwa Bani ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf na kuanzishwa kwa msikiti hapo."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "He rode on with people walking beside him until his camel knelt at the site of the mosque in Madinah."
msgstr "Alipanda mnyama huku watu wakitembea kando yake hadi ngamia wake alipopiga magoti kwenye eneo la msikiti huko Madinah."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "It does not establish the route taken through the town or the appearance of the place."
msgstr "Haionyeshi njia iliyopitwa ndani ya mji au jinsi eneo hilo lilivyokuwa linaonekana."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "This excerpt does not give an exact departure date."
msgstr "Dondoo hili halitaji tarehe kamili ya kuondoka."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The excerpt describes preparations, not a nightly delivery to the cave."
msgstr "Dondoo hili linaeleza maandalizi, si uwasilishaji wa usiku kwenye pango."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The excerpt does not describe erasing footprints."
msgstr "Dondoo hili halielezi kufutwa kwa nyayo za miguu."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The account does not describe the cave’s dimensions or layout."
msgstr "Simulizi haielezi vipimo au mpangilio wa pango."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "This excerpt is not the full verse and does not itself name Abu Bakr or Mount Thawr."
msgstr "Dondoo hili si aya nzima na lenyewe halimtaji Abu Bakr wala Mlima Thawr."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "This is Ibn Kathir’s commentary, not the Quranic wording itself."
msgstr "Huu ni ufafanuzi wa Ibn Kathir, si maneno yenyewe ya Quran."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "It does not give an exact location for the stay among Bani ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf."
msgstr "Haitoi eneo kamili la makazi miongoni mwa Bani ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The passage does not name the place; identifying it as Quba rests on other reports."
msgstr "Kifungu hiki hakitaji jina la eneo hilo; kulitambua kama Quba kunategemea ripoti zingine."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The night of departure"
msgstr "Usiku wa kuondoka"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The leaders of Quraysh met in Dar al-Nadwah, the house where they settled their affairs, to decide what to do about the Prophet ﷺ now that they feared him."
msgstr "Viongozi wa Quraysh walikutana Dar al-Nadwah, nyumba waliyokuwa wakiamulia mambo yao, ili kuamua nini cha kufanya kuhusu Mtume ﷺ sasa kwa kuwa walikuwa wakimhofia."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "That night they gathered at his door, waiting for him to sleep. He told ‘Ali to lie in his bed, wrapped in his green cloak, and assured him that no harm from them would reach him."
msgstr "Usiku huo walikusanyika mlangoni kwake, wakimsubiri alale. Akamwambia ‘Ali alale kitandani kwake, akiwa amejifunika joho lake la kijani, na akamhakikishia kuwa hakuna madhara yoyote kutoka kwao yatakayomfikia."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The tent of Umm Ma‘bad"
msgstr "Hema la Umm Ma‘bad"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq reports that Quraysh met in Dar al-Nadwah to consult about the Prophet ﷺ once they feared him."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq anaripoti kuwa Quraysh walikutana Dar al-Nadwah ili kushauriana kuhusu Mtume ﷺ mara tu walipomhofia."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The excerpt covers the meeting, not what was said in it."
msgstr "Dondoo hili linahusu mkutano wenyewe, si yale yaliyosemwa humo."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "They gathered at his door at night; he told ‘Ali to sleep in his bed under his green cloak and assured him of safety."
msgstr "Walikusanyika mlangoni kwake usiku; akamwambia ‘Ali alale kitandani kwake chini ya joho lake la kijani na akamhakikishia usalama."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Kathir notes that al-Waqidi also relates this, combining several narrators’ accounts."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir anabainisha kuwa al-Waqidi pia anasimulia hili, akichanganya masimulizi ya wasimulizi kadhaa."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq introduces this with “as it has reached me”."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq anaanza kueleza hili kwa kusema \"kama ilivyonifikia\"."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Kathir calls the story well known, through routes that support one another. It does not fix where the tent stood."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir analitaja kisa hiki kuwa kinajulikana sana, kupitia njia zinazosaidiana zenyewe kwa zenyewe. Hakitaji wapi hema hilo lilipokuwa limesimama."

#: src/content/details.js
#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "Al-Rahiq al-Makhtum"
msgstr "Al-Rahiq al-Makhtum"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The noon visit"
msgstr "Ziara ya mchana"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "At the height of noon, an hour at which he never used to come, the Prophet ﷺ arrived at Abu Bakr’s house with his face covered. He said he had been given permission to leave. Abu Bakr asked to go with him, and he said yes."
msgstr "Wakati wa mchana wa jua kali, saa ambayo hakuwa na kawaida ya kuja, Mtume ﷺ alifika nyumbani kwa Abu Bakr akiwa amefunika uso wake. Alisema amepewa ruhusa ya kuondoka. Abu Bakr aliomba kuondoka naye, naye akakubali."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "This is ‘Aishah’s account as quoted in a modern sirah. The position of the house is illustrative."
msgstr "Huu ni usimulizi wa 'Aishah kama ulivyonukuliwa katika sirah ya kisasa. Mahali pa nyumba ni kwa ajili ya kuonyesha tu."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Stones in the niche"
msgstr "Mawe kwenye tundu la ukutani"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money with him, five or six thousand dirhams. Asma recounts that her blind grandfather feared the family had been left with nothing. She put stones where the money used to be kept, covered them with a cloth, and guided his hand to them so that he would be at ease."
msgstr "Abu Bakr alichukua pesa zake zote, dirham elfu tano au sita. Asma anasimulia kwamba babu yake kipofu alihofia kuwa familia imeachwa bila kitu. Aliweka mawe mahali ambapo pesa zilikuwa zikiwekwa, akayafunika kwa nguo, na kuuongoza mkono wake hadi kwenye mawe hayo ili apate utulivu."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Reported by Ibn Ishaq from Asma through her grandson. The position of the house is illustrative."
msgstr "Imeripotiwa na Ibn Ishaq kutoka kwa Asma kupitia mjukuu wake. Mahali pa nyumba ni kwa ajili ya kuonyesha tu."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Why south?"
msgstr "Kwa nini kusini?"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Madinah lies to the north, and that is where a search would begin. They left in the opposite direction, on the road towards Yemen, for about five miles to Mount Thawr."
msgstr "Madinah iko upande wa kaskazini, na huko ndiko utafutaji ungeanzia. Waliondoka kuelekea upande wa pili, kwenye barabara inayoelekea Yemen, kwa takriban maili tano hadi Mlima Thawr."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "This is a modern author’s reading of the route, not wording from an early report."
msgstr "Huku ni kusoma kwa mwandishi wa kisasa kuhusu njia hiyo, si maneno kutoka kwenye ripoti ya mapema."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "She of the two belts"
msgstr "Mwenye mikanda miwili"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "When the three nights had passed, Asma brought their provisions but had forgotten a strap to hang the bag. She undid her waist-belt and used it. For that she was called Dhat al-Nitaqayn, she of the two belts."
msgstr "Zilipopita usiku tatu, Asma alileta chakula chao lakini alikuwa amesahau kamba ya kuning'inizia mfuko. Alifungua mkanda wake wa kiunoni na kuutumia. Kwa ajili hiyo aliitwa Dhat al-Nitaqayn, mwenye mikanda miwili."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq’s report. ‘Aishah’s account in al-Bukhari places the belt at the packing of the provisions instead."
msgstr "Ripoti ya Ibn Ishaq. Usimulizi wa 'Aishah katika al-Bukhari unaweka mkanda huo wakati wa kufungasha chakula badala yake."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The spider’s web"
msgstr "Utando wa buibui"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "One report says the pursuers climbed the mountain, passed the cave, and saw a spider’s web across its opening. No one could have gone in, they reasoned, and they moved on. Ibn Kathir calls its chain good, the best of what is reported on this. The scene does not draw the web."
msgstr "Ripoti moja inasema wafuatiliaji walipanda mlima, wakapita pango, na kuona utando wa buibui kwenye mdomo wake. Walisema hakuna mtu ambaye angeingia, na wakaendelea mbele. Ibn Kathir anasema mnyororo wake wa wapokezi ni mzuri, bora zaidi kati ya yale yaliyoripotiwa kuhusu hili. Mandhari haya hayachori utando huo."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "A single report. The nesting doves of popular retellings are not part of it."
msgstr "Ripoti moja tu. Njiwa wanaotaga mayai wa hadithi maarufu si sehemu yake."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The stations of the road"
msgstr "Vituo vya njiani"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq names the way the guide took: below Makkah, along the coast, across the road below ‘Usfan, below Amaj, past Qudayd, then al-Kharrar, Thaniyyat al-Marah, Liqf and on. Many of these names are hard to place today, so the line drawn here stays approximate."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq anataja njia ambayo kiongozi alichukua: chini ya Makkah, kando ya pwani, kuvuka barabara chini ya 'Usfan, chini ya Amaj, kupita Qudayd, kisha al-Kharrar, Thaniyyat al-Marah, Liqf na kuendelea. Majina mengi kati ya haya ni vigumu kuyatafuta leo, kwa hiyo mstari uliorandishwa hapa unabaki wa makadirio tu."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "A list of names, without distances or days."
msgstr "Orodha ya majina, bila umbali au siku."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "White garments"
msgstr "Nguo nyeupe"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "On the way they met al-Zubayr with a group of Muslim merchants returning from Syria. He gave the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr white garments to wear."
msgstr "Njiani walikutana na al-Zubayr akiwa na kundi la wafanyabiashara wa Kiislamu wakirejea kutoka Syria. Alimpa Mtume ﷺ na Abu Bakr nguo nyeupe za kuvaa."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "From al-Bukhari, as quoted by Ibn Kathir. The account does not say where on the road they met."
msgstr "Kutoka al-Bukhari, kama ilivyonukuliwa na Ibn Kathir. Usimulizi huo hausemi ni wapi njiani walipokutana."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The first Friday"
msgstr "Ijumaa ya kwanza"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "After leaving Quba, the time for Friday prayer came while he was among Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf. He led it there, in the mosque in the bed of the valley, with about a hundred men."
msgstr "Baada ya kuondoka Quba, wakati wa swala ya Ijumaa ulifika akiwa miongoni mwa Banu Salim ibn 'Awf. Aliongoza swala hapo, katika msikiti ulioko kwenye bonde, akiwa na wanaume takriban mia moja."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Quoted from a modern sirah, which cites Ibn Hisham. The position is illustrative."
msgstr "Imenukuliwa kutoka kwenye sirah ya kisasa, ambayo inataja Ibn Hisham. Mahali hapa ni kwa ajili ya kuonyesha tu."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Let her go"
msgstr "Mwacheni aende"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Clan after clan took hold of his camel’s rope and invited him to stay with them. Each time he answered: let her go, for she is under command. She walked on until she knelt in the quarter of Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."
msgstr "Ukoo baada ya ukoo ulishika kamba ya ngamia wake na kumwalika akae nao. Kila mara alijibu: mwacheni aende, kwani yuko chini ya amri. Alitembea hadi akapiga magoti katika robo ya Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq’s report. Her path through the town is not known."
msgstr "Ripoti ya Ibn Ishaq. Njia yake kupitia mji haijulikani."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The house of Abu Ayyub"
msgstr "Nyumba ya Abu Ayyub"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "He stayed in the house of Abu Ayyub until his mosque and his rooms were built, and he worked on the building himself alongside the Muhajirun and the Ansar."
msgstr "Alikaa katika nyumba ya Abu Ayyub hadi msikiti wake na vyumba vyake vilipojengwa, na alifanya kazi ya ujenzi mwenyewe pamoja na Muhajirun na Ansar."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The house is placed beside the mosque site for illustration."
msgstr "Nyumba imewekwa kando ya eneo la msikiti kwa ajili ya kuonyesha tu."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Brothers"
msgstr "Ndugu"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "He paired those who had migrated with those who received them, as brothers, so that each newcomer had someone to lean on."
msgstr "Aliwaunganisha wale waliohamia na wale waliowapokea, kama ndugu, ili kila mgeni awe na mtu wa kumtegemea."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "This is Ibn Kathir’s chapter heading. The individual pairings are listed in the pages that follow it."
msgstr "Hiki ni kichwa cha sura ya Ibn Kathir. Muunganisho wa mmoja mmoja umeorodheshwa katika kurasa zinazofuata."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The full moon has risen"
msgstr "Mwezi mpevu umechomoza juu yetu"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "A well-known report says the women and children sang “The full moon has risen upon us, from the passes of al-Wada‘” when he arrived. Al-Bayhaqi relates it from Ibn ‘Aishah, a later narrator, not from someone who was there."
msgstr "Simulizi inayojulikana sana inasema kwamba wanawake na watoto waliimba \"Mwezi mpevu umetuchomozea, kutoka mapito ya al-Wada‘\" alipowasili. Al-Bayhaqi anaipokea kutoka kwa Ibn ‘Aishah, mpokezi wa baadaye, si kutoka kwa mtu aliyekuwepo hapo."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The chain stops short of an eyewitness, and some place the song at a later return to Madinah, not at this arrival."
msgstr "Mlolongo wa wapokezi unaishia kabla ya kumfikia shuhuda wa macho, na baadhi ya watu wanaweka wimbo huo katika kurejea kwa baadaye huko Madinah, si katika kuwasili huku."

