#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
msgid "Cave model: <0/>"
msgstr "Kielelezo cha pango: <0/>"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Ali was told to stay behind until he had returned the deposits people had left with the Prophet ﷺ."
msgstr "‘Ali aliambiwa abaki nyuma hadi arejeshe amana ambazo watu walikuwa wamemwekea Mtume ﷺ."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The searchers came so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” The Prophet ﷺ answered, “What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Watafutaji walikaribia sana kiasi kwamba Abu Bakr alinong'ona, “Kama mmoja wao angetazama chini miguuni pake, angetuona.” Mtume ﷺ akajibu, “Unaonaje kuhusu wawili ambao Allah ni wa tatu wao?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Allah recalled this moment in the Quran: “the second of two, when they were in the cave, when he said to his companion, ‘Do not grieve; Allah is with us.’”"
msgstr "Allah alikumbusha wakati huu katika Quran: “wa pili wa wawili, walipokuwa katika pango, alipomwambia swahaba wake, ‘Usihuzunike; hakika Allah yu pamoja nasi.’”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Ibn Ishaq’s telling, when the three nights had passed, Asma brought their food but had no strap to hang the bag. She undid her waist-belt and tied it on, and so she was called She of the Two Belts."
msgstr "Katika masimulizi ya Ibn Ishaq, usiku hizo tatu zilipopita, Asma aliwaletea chakula lakini hakuwa na kamba ya kuning'inizia mfuko huo. Alifungua mkanda wake wa kiunoni na kuufungia, na ndipo akaitwa Mwenye Mikanda Miwili."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The pursuers climbed the mountain and passed the cave. Seeing a spider’s web across its opening, they said no one could have gone in there, and moved on. Ibn Kathir calls this report’s chain good."
msgstr "Waliokuwa wakiwafuata walipanda mlima na kupita penye pango. Walipoona utando wa buibui ukiwa umetanda mlangoni pake, walisema hakuna mtu ambaye angeweza kuingia humo, wakaendelea mbele. Ibn Kathir anasema mlolongo wa upokezi wa riwaya hii ni mzuri."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Some tell that the searchers saw a spider’s web across the cave’s opening, and walked on."
msgstr "Wengine wanasimulia kwamba watafutaji waliona utando wa buibui kwenye mlango wa pango, wakaendelea na njia yao."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Bukhari gives three nights. Which nights of the week they were comes from a later biography."
msgstr "Al-Bukhari anataja kuwa zilikuwa usiku tatu. Zilikuwa usiku zipi za juma, maelezo hayo yanatoka kwenye wasifu wa baadaye."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how the two reached a cave on Mount Thawr and hid there for three nights."
msgstr "‘Aishah anasimulia jinsi wawili hao walivyofika kwenye pango katika Mlima Thawr na kujificha humo kwa usiku tatu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how her brother ‘Abdullah spent the nights with them and brought them news from Makkah after dark."
msgstr "‘Aishah anasimulia jinsi kaka yake ‘Abdullah alivyolala nao usiku na kuwaletea habari kutoka Makkah baada ya giza kuingia."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought the ewes to the cave each evening of the three nights."
msgstr "‘Aishah anasimulia jinsi ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah alivyowaleta kondoo jike pangoni kila jioni ya zile usiku tatu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr recalls fearing that anyone who looked down at his own feet would see them."
msgstr "Abu Bakr anakumbuka jinsi alivyohofia kwamba yeyote angetazama chini miguuni pake angewashuhudia."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The verse speaks of the Prophet ﷺ as the second of two in the cave, telling his companion not to grieve."
msgstr "Aya hiyo inamtaja Mtume ﷺ akiwa wa pili wa wawili pangoni, akimwambia swahaba wake asihuzunike."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir explains the verse: Allah supported and aided His Messenger, who sheltered in the cave for three days."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir anaifafanua aya hiyo: Allah alimsaidia na kumnusuru Mtume Wake, aliyejificha pangoni kwa siku tatu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how Asma tied the food bag with her waist-belt, and so was called She of the Two Belts."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq anasimulia jinsi Asma alivyofunga mfuko wa chakula kwa mkanda wake wa kiunoni, na hivyo akaitwa Mwenye Mikanda Miwili."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The report of the spider’s web across the cave’s opening, whose chain Ibn Kathir calls good."
msgstr "Riwaya ya utando wa buibui kwenye mlango wa pango, ambayo mlolongo wake wa upokezi Ibn Kathir anauita mzuri."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A modern biography names the three nights: the nights before Friday, Saturday and Sunday."
msgstr "Wasifu wa kisasa unazitaja usiku hizo tatu: usiku wa kuamkia Ijumaa, Jumamosi, na Jumapili."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
msgid "The number beside each book counts its source passages."
msgstr "Namba kando ya kila kitabu ni idadi ya vifungu vyake vya marejeo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr reached a cave on Mount Thawr and hid inside it. They would stay there for three nights."
msgstr "Mtume ﷺ na Abu Bakr walifika kwenye pango katika Mlima Thawr na wakajificha ndani yake. Walikaa humo kwa usiku tatu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each night, Abu Bakr’s son ‘Abdullah slept near them. Before dawn he slipped back to Makkah, so that morning found him among Quraysh as if he had never left, and at dark he returned with any plot he had heard."
msgstr "Kila usiku, mwana wa Abu Bakr, ‘Abdullah, alilala karibu nao. Kabla ya alfajiri, alirejea Makkah kisirisiri, kiasi kwamba asubuhi ilimkuta miongoni mwa Quraysh kana kwamba hakuwahi kuondoka, na kulipogiza alirudi akiwa na taarifa za njama yoyote aliyoisikia."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah grazed a few milking ewes nearby and brought them to the cave after nightfall, so the two had milk. He did this on each of the three nights."
msgstr "Mtumwa aliyeachwa huru na Abu Bakr, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, alichunga kondoo jike wachache wa maziwa karibu na hapo na kuwaleta pangoni baada ya giza kuingia, ili wawili hao wapate maziwa. Alifanya hivyo katika kila usiku wa siku hizo tatu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr slipped into a cave on Mount Thawr and stayed out of sight. For three nights, it would be their hiding place."
msgstr "Mtume ﷺ na Abu Bakr waliingia kisiri kwenye pango la Mlima Thawr na kujificha. Kwa muda wa usiku tatu, pango hilo lingekuwa maficho yao."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They were not alone for long. Each night Abu Bakr’s son ‘Abdullah came after dark with whatever Quraysh were plotting, then slipped back before dawn, so that morning found him in Makkah as if he had never left."
msgstr "Hawakukaa peke yao kwa muda mrefu. Kila usiku baada ya giza kuingia, mwana wa Abu Bakr, ‘Abdullah, aliwajia na habari za mipango ya Quraysh. Kisha alirudi kisiri kabla ya mapambazuko, ili alfajiri imkute Makkah kana kwamba hakuwa ameondoka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "And as darkness settled, Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought a few milking ewes to the cave, so the two had fresh milk. Every one of the three nights, he came."
msgstr "Giza lilipoingia, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, mtumwa aliyeachiliwa huru wa Abu Bakr, alileta kondoo wachache wa kukamuliwa pangoni, ili hao wawili wapate maziwa freshi. Alikuja katika kila mmoja wa usiku huo mitatu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the searchers came close, so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” The Prophet ﷺ answered, “What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Kisha waliokuwa wakiwatafuta wakakaribia, karibu sana hivi kwamba Abu Bakr akanong’ona, “Kama mmoja wao angeangalia chini ya miguu yake, angetuona.” Mtume ﷺ akajibu, “Unaonaje wawili ambao Allah yuko pamoja nao akiwa wa tatu?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Allah preserved that moment in the Quran: “the second of two, when they were in the cave, when he said to his companion, ‘Do not grieve; Allah is with us.’”"
msgstr "Allah aliihifadhi pindi hiyo katika Qur’ani: “wa pili kati ya wawili, walipokuwa pangoni, alipomwambia mwenzake, ‘Usihuzunike; hakika Allah yuko pamoja nasi.’”"
